    "body": "## What changed\n\n`_extract_session_llm` (the env-gated M2 lane) shared `_CAPTURE_PASSTHROUGH_PROPS` with the v2 seam but built the response `props` by filtering the **folded statement dict**, with no read-back \u2014 on both the create and the in-capture-fold path. The v2 seam (#2949) persists the four E3 fields on create and, on a dedup hit, reads the canonical's **stored** props back. The M2 lane did neither.\n\n**The latent gap is real, and wider than the issue body recorded.** Probed on the embedded lane with a fake extractor calling `EventAPI.add_point(..., quote=, when=, source_turn_id=, search_keys=[...], span_start=, span_end=)`:\n\n| Path | Before (payload echo) | Graph held |\n|---|---|---|\n| create | `search_keys: [\"alpha\",\"beta\"]` advertised | **no `search_keys`** \u2014 the projection drops undeclared list props (`_POINT_LIST_PROPS` is empty, #2795 D2; no `_flatten_search_keys_prop` on that door) \u2192 the #2813 symptom verbatim |\n| fold | the **duplicate's** `quote`/`when`/`source_turn_id` advertised | the **canonical's** values (the duplicate node is detached) |\n\n### Fix (issue Option 1, in its truthful form)\n\nRead the stored props back through the **same** `_read_capture_passthrough_props` helper the v2 dedup-hit lane uses \u2014 the F4-derived read-back whose field list comes from `_CAPTURE_PASSTHROUGH_ORDER` \u2014 for **every** entry, create and fold alike. One contract for both capture lanes: the reply describes the graph. Absent (not stored) fields are omitted, never fabricated; a vanished node fails CLOSED to `{}`. Reading back rather than re-deriving write-side presence rules by hand keeps the projection's policy the single owner of what is persisted (that duplication is exactly the drift #2949 review F4 removed).\n\nAlso updated the shared E3 owner note (removing the residual \"M2 folded statement dict / no read-back\" claim \u2014 the issue's Secondary item) and the seam docstring: `props` is the **stored subset**, not a payload superset.\n\n`tortoise/sdk.py`, `tests/test_capture_session.py`.\n\n## Test evidence\n\n```\n# full file + the #3945 sibling (embedded lane)\nTORTOISE_TEST_CARVE_OUT=1 HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n    tests/test_capture_session.py tests/test_capture_validfrom_3945.py -q -p no:cacheprovider\n203 passed, 1 skipped, 1 warning in 213.33s\n```\n\nNew tests (M2 branch section) \u2014 `18 passed, 184 deselected` for `-k \"extract_session_llm or passthrough or read_clause or read_helper\"`:\n\n```\npytest tests/test_capture_session.py -k \"extract_session_llm or passthrough or read_clause or read_helper\" -q\n18 passed, 184 deselected, 1 warning in 40.68s\n```\n\n* `test_extract_session_llm_reports_stored_props_not_the_folded_payload` \u2014 create path reports the stored props; `search_keys` absent (the projection never persisted it).\n* `test_extract_session_llm_fold_reports_the_canonicals_stored_props` \u2014 the folded entry reports the canonical's stored values, not the duplicate's.\n* `test_extract_session_llm_in_tree_lane_advertises_nothing_unstored` \u2014 parity pin: the real in-tree M2 extractor's entries stay `{}` because the nodes hold none (no behaviour change for the shipped lane).\n\n**Mutation arms verified** (fix temporarily reverted to the payload echo, both RED, then restored byte-identical):\n\n```\nE  AssertionError: {'quote': 'q top', ..., 'search_keys': ['alpha','beta'], ...}\nE    Left contains 1 more item: {'search_keys': ['alpha', 'beta']}\nE  assert {'quote': 'q second', 'when': '2026-08-02', 'source_turn_id': 'turn-2'} == {'quote': 'q first', 'when': '2026-08-01', 'source_turn_id': 'turn-1'}\nFAILED ..._reports_stored_props_not_the_folded_payload\nFAILED ..._fold_reports_the_canonicals_stored_props\n2 failed, 1 warning in 10.70s\n```\n\nAlso: `ruff check tortoise/sdk.py tests/test_capture_session.py` \u2192 All checks passed; `tools/ci_selection.py --integrity` \u2192 all test files classified, shards consistent (no new test file, nothing to register); `py_compile` on both changed files OK.\n\n## Pre-existing bug filed\n\n**#8006** \u2014 the projection door silently drops a declared list-valued `search_keys` (log-only warning; contradicts `_flatten_search_keys_prop`'s docstring, which says the projection flattens per R2 D3), so the E3 alias field cannot ride `EventAPI.add_point` at all. Found while measuring this issue; not in scope here (this PR makes the *reply* truthful about it).\n\n## Not changed\n\nNo MCP tool registry or public `TortoiseSDK` surface change.\n\nCloses #3778\n\nreview recorded: reviews/8007.json verdict=clean @ f66c912f3e364181b429997c81d3cfcc40e14821 diff=6cc2c187fb50728c5e1141292c7d48efd569429af3c1c87e0db34a7808106037 (daniel-ospina/tortoise) sig=954f6ce4966f6b00fd3349530b96c3e4082518c47cebe0021c07dda3f1fb1104",
